  "notes": "⛔ **The only entry in this batch that leaves half-time.** The research says his records frequently sit in a dancehall/afro-leaning straight feel rather than trap's half-time, so `session.halfTime` is false, the tempo band drops to 100–140, and `snare.fullTimeVariantProb` is 0.5 — the riddim-derived backbeat lands on about half the seeds and trap's beat-3 clap on the rest. Everything else is restraint: hats in 8ths at `fillDensity` 0.3 with almost no rolls (\"never doing too much\" is a stated rule), light rim/shaker/woodblock percussion, one repeated melodic cell at `densityPerBar` [2,5] with `loopVerbatim`, and a real chord bed with R&B sevenths and ninths, which is unusual for this genre. The sub plays a slow melodic line *under* the chords, so the bass is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.5 with `melodicallyIndependent` set. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium, and because `halfTime: false` is the biggest single inference here — the research names the feel, not a grid.",
